enchland gravels, picked early for cassis, red currant and violet rather than jam. Bay leaf, Rutherford-style dust and cedar sit over fine, insistent tannins and lively acidity, and the wine ages with real grace.","x":"284:2,285:70,286:68,287:65,288:65,289:70,290:82,291:40,292:0,293:20,13:80,6:40,14:50,2:30,9:30,71:35,72:15,159:45,156:15,142:35,153:45,105:30,104:25,97:20,114:20,119:20,214:75,212:35,230:45,236:90,249:70,258:80,245:65,240:55,252:45,282:90,279:55,295:100,294:100,299:100,310:100,315:100"},{"s":"dunn-vineyards-howell-mountain-cabernet-sauvignon","n":"Howell Mountain Cabernet Sauvignon","p":"Dunn Vineyards","t":"red","c":"USA","r":"Napa Valley","a":"Howell Mountain","g":["Cabernet Sauvignon"],"pr":135,"abv":14,"e":"About 30 months in French oak, around half new","sv":"17–18°C","d":"3–4 hours when young","w":"15–40 years from vintage","ds":"Mountain Cabernet of the old, unyielding school: dense blackcurrant and blackberry locked behind iron, graphite and volcanic-soil dust. The tannins are massive and grippy in youth, the alcohol deliberately moderate, and patience of a decade or more is part of the price of admission.","x":"284:2,285:60,286:95,287:65,288:85,289:80,290:85,291:50,292:0,293:15,13:80,12:75,15:40,16:30,142:55,140:50,143:35,153:40,151:30,159:45,186:25,126:30,112:20,168:20,105:20,216:90,220:40,227:55,239:60,251:75,237:80,245:95,255:80,246:30,258:55,282:100,279:70,294:100,295:100,297:100,315:100"},{"s":"kosta-browne-russian-river-valley-pinot-noir","n":"Russian River Valley Pinot Noir","p":"Kosta Browne","t":"red","c":"USA","r":"Sonoma County","a":"Russian River Valley","g":["Pinot Noir"],"pr":95,"abv":14.3,"e":"About 16 months in French oak, roughly 45% new","sv":"14–16°C","d":"Not needed; 20 minutes helps","w":"Now–8 years","ds":"Russian River Pinot at its most voluptuous: black cherry, raspberry and cola spun into a plush, satiny palate with toasty vanilla and cinnamon. Ripe and glossy, it trades Burgundian tension for sheer generosity of fruit.","x":"284:4,285:55,286:38,287:75,288:65,289:85,290:70,291:55,292:0,293:12,14:85,3:65,1:55,21:50,9:45,165:55,156:50,157:35,135:45,124:20,72:20,148:20,158:15,212:65,226:80,229:55,224:50,238:80,244:85,241:80,257:70,247:75,250:70,259:55,279:70,283:50,304:100,299:100,310:100,296:100"},{"s":"rombauer-carneros-chardonnay","n":"Carneros Chardonnay","p":"Rombauer Vineyards","t":"white","c":"USA","r":"Napa Valley","a":"Carneros","g":["Chardonnay"],"pr":42,"abv":14.5,"e":"Barrel-fermented with full malolactic, about 9 months sur lie in French and American oak","sv":"10–12°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–3 years","ds":"The benchmark for buttery California Chardonnay: melted butter, vanilla custard and butterscotch over ripe peach, baked apple and pineapple. Creamy, broad and low in acid, it is pure comfort in a glass and makes no pretence of austerity.","x":"284:8,285:40,286:2,287:80,288:85,289:85,290:65,291:65,292:0,293:12,176:95,177:60,156:75,157:45,172:50,171:25,160:20,47:50,33:50,49:45,54:55,58:40,59:30,43:35,221:90,226:70,224:75,223:35,238:90,257:70,241:80,244:70,250:80,256:70,259:55,266:45,283:80,279:50,305:100,312:100,298:100,303:100"},{"s":"hanzell-vineyards-sonoma-valley-chardonnay","n":"Sonoma Valley Chardonnay","p":"Hanzell Vineyards","t":"white","c":"USA","r":"Sonoma County","a":"Sonoma Valley","g":["Chardonnay"],"pr":85,"abv":14,"e":"Malolactic blocked; fermented and aged about a year in French oak, roughly a third new, with some steel","sv":"11–13°C","d":"30 minutes when young","w":"5–20 years from vintage","ds":"Old-vine Sonoma Chardonnay that refuses the butter path: with malolactic blocked, lemon, green apple and quince stay taut over wet stone and a flinty edge. Tightly wound when young, it gains hazelnut and beeswax over a decade and remains one of California''s longest-lived whites.","x":"284:2,285:78,286:3,287:65,288:70,289:75,290:85,291:40,292:0,293:20,34:70,40:50,46:55,47:40,49:45,51:30,53:30,45:25,136:65,137:35,141:30,203:25,157:20,193:15,85:20,230:70,22