h a reductive flicker of struck match and flint. Lean and saline through the middle, it finishes long and stony, closer to Puligny than to Napa.","x":"284:2,285:78,286:3,287:55,288:60,289:68,290:72,291:30,292:0,293:15,34:70,40:40,46:50,47:30,49:40,53:30,36:15,147:45,137:40,136:50,141:25,203:25,157:20,85:20,79:15,230:60,228:55,225:35,221:20,249:75,243:65,236:70,240:75,268:50,260:40,266:35,279:70,282:55,303:100,305:100,298:100,310:100"},{"s":"leonetti-cellar-cabernet-sauvignon","n":"Cabernet Sauvignon","p":"Leonetti Cellar","t":"red","c":"USA","r":"Walla Walla Valley","a":"Walla Walla Valley","g":["Cabernet Sauvignon","Merlot","Petit Verdot","Malbec"],"pr":125,"abv":14.5,"e":"About 22 months in French oak, a high proportion new","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1–2 hours when young","w":"8–25 years from vintage","ds":"Washington''s founding cult Cabernet: dense cassis, black cherry and plum layered with mocha, cedar and a graphite edge. Concentrated and polished, its ripe fruit is held by a firm, velvety frame that rewards cellaring.","x":"284:3,285:62,286:78,287:75,288:85,289:85,290:85,291:65,292:0,293:15,13:80,14:70,12:60,15:40,16:20,167:45,168:35,156:45,157:40,159:45,142:30,126:25,135:30,153:20,104:20,213:60,219:55,227:30,255:80,237:65,247:75,245:80,238:50,248:60,259:65,282:90,279:65,294:100,295:100,297:100,315:100"},{"s":"cayuse-vineyards-cailloux-vineyard-syrah","n":"Cailloux Vineyard Syrah","p":"Cayuse Vineyards","t":"red","c":"USA","r":"Walla Walla Valley","a":"The Rocks District of Milton-Freewater","g":["Syrah"],"pr":150,"abv":14,"e":"Native fermentation with some whole clusters; about 20 months in neutral French barrels and puncheons","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1–2 hours","w":"5–20 years from vintage","ds":"Biodynamic Syrah from cobblestone vineyards that taste of the ground they grow in: smoked meat, black olive, iron and crushed rock first, blackberry and violet second. Wild, savory and intensely perfumed, it divides tables and enthralls those who love it.","x":"284:2,285:60,286:55,287:70,288:80,289:95,290:85,291:25,292:0,293:15,190:90,112:75,188:55,196:50,143:45,140:50,12:60,21:40,16:30,120:60,71:45,126:20,104:20,149:15,155:30,227:40,214:45,226:40,242:90,253:55,255:75,237:55,248:85,252:55,243:50,262:40,260:55,265:40,282:80,279:50,295:100,297:100,300:100,301:100,299:100"},{"s":"charles-smith-boom-boom-syrah","n":"Boom Boom! Syrah","p":"Charles Smith Wines","t":"red","c":"USA","r":"Columbia Valley","a":"Columbia Valley","g":["Syrah"],"pr":18,"abv":13.5,"e":"About 10 months in stainless steel and older French oak","sv":"15–17°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–3 years","ds":"Loud label, generous glass: blackberry, blueberry and plum with cracked pepper and a hint of smoky bacon. Soft-edged, juicy and dark-fruited, it is a reliable weeknight Syrah built to please.","x":"284:8,285:55,286:45,287:70,288:68,289:72,290:55,291:30,292:0,293:10,12:75,16:60,15:50,14:45,120:55,190:30,71:30,126:20,112:15,156:25,167:20,226:50,229:60,213:35,244:85,256:90,241:65,250:60,260:30,279:85,283:90,300:100,302:100,296:100,309:100,311:100"},{"s":"hermann-j-wiemer-dry-riesling","n":"Dry Riesling","p":"Hermann J. Wiemer","t":"white","c":"USA","r":"Finger Lakes","a":"Seneca Lake","g":["Riesling"],"pr":22,"abv":12,"e":"Native-yeast fermentation in stainless steel and older casks, aged on fine lees","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–10 years","ds":"The Finger Lakes'' benchmark dry Riesling: lime, green apple and white peach over wet stone and slate from the shores of Seneca Lake. Bracing acidity and only a whisper of residual sugar make it taut, mineral and endlessly versatile at the table.","x":"284:10,285:90,286:0,287:40,288:38,289:70,290:70,291:0,292:0,293:12,35:75,34:50,40:40,46:65,53:45,36:30,55:20,139:55,136:70,141:25,74:30,85:30,191:10,129:10,228:80,230:70,225:50,229:45,240:90,249:75,243:75,258:65,261:70,282:55,279:75,308:100,307:100,296:100,305:100,306:100"},{"s":"textbook-paso-robles-cabernet-sauvignon","n":"Paso Robles Cabernet Sauvignon","p":"Textbook","t":"red","c":"USA","r":"Paso Robles","a":"Paso Robles","g":["Cabernet Sauvignon","Petite Sirah"],"pr":30,"abv":13.9,"e":"About 14 months in French oak, roughly a third new; stainless-steel fermentation","sv":"16–18°C","d":"30 minutes","w":"Now–6 years","ds":"A Napa house''s take on Paso: dark cherry, blackberry and cassis with plum and a red-currant lift, framed by cedar, tobacco leaf and baking spice from French oak. Riper and rounder than a Bordeaux, more restrained than a Napa blockbuster — firm but approachable tannins and enough acidity to keep it from feeling heavy.","x":"284:5,285:55,286:60,287:60,288:70,289:70,290:60,291:50,292:0,293:15,14:80,12:70,13:60,15:55,9:45,1:35,6:35,3:25,159:50,119:45,164:30,156:30,157:25,135:45,127:30,107:20,168:40,169:30,213:50,216:30,231:50,224:40,229:35,244:60,241:55,256:65,250:55,245:50,258:50,247:50,248:40,237:35,259:30,279:60,283:50,294:100,295:100,300:100,302:100,315:100"},{"s":"torbreck-woodcutters-shiraz","n":"Woodcutter''s Shiraz","p":"Torbreck","t":"red","c":"Australia","r":"South Australia","a":"Barossa Valley","g":["Shiraz"],"pr":25,"abv":15,"e":"About 12 months in large, seasoned French oak foudres","sv":"16–18°C","d":"30–60 minutes","w":"Now–8 years","ds":"Barossa warmth in a glass: blackberry, plum and mulberry poured over dark chocolate and licorice, with a gentle lick of pepper. Large old casks keep the oak out of the way, so the fruit arrives plush, generous and ready to drink.","x":"284:4,285:45,286:60,287:80,288:85,289:82,290:70,291:30,292:0,293:15,12:90,15:70,16:40,17:35,28:35,168:70,126:65,120:35,135:30,167:30,156:20,143:15,98:12,226:75,213:60,224:40,238:80,241:75,244:70,250:70,256:60,260:55,279:70,283:55,300:100,294:100,302:100,315:100"},{"s":"yangarra-estate-old-vine-grenache","n":"Old Vine Grenache","p":"Yangarra Estate Vineyard","t":"red","c":"Australia","r":"South Australia","a":"McLaren Vale","g":["Grenache"],"pr":38,"abv":14.5,"e":"Wild-fermented with some whole bunches; about 10 months in seasoned large-format French oak","sv":"14–16°C","d":"30 minutes","w":"Now–12 years","ds":"Bush vines planted in the 1940s on the deep sands of Blewitt Springs give Grenache of real perfume: raspberry, red cherry and rose petal laced with garrigue and white pepper. The tannins are fine and sandy, the fruit juicy rather than heavy, a long way from the jammy Grenache of old.","x":"284:3,285:55,286:50,287:72,288:62,289:75,290:72,291:15,292:0,293:18,3:85,1:70,9:45,4:35,8:30,72:35,71:20,106:50,111:30,121:35,134:30,127:15,152:25,153:30,214:60,212:45,229:60,231:50,252:75,236:65,240:60,262:35,260:50,278:80,265:30,279:60,282:45,295:100,299:100,301:100,314:100"}]'::jsonb);
